---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../config/site";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = `Topics | ${SITE.name}`;
const description =
  "Choose the right finance topic hub for APR, credit-card payoff, DTI, rent vs buy, mortgage payoff, and refinance decisions. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-06-24";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/topics"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Topics</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Topics: choose the right finance workflow</h1>
    <p>
      This page is the top routing layer for the site's main finance clusters. Use it when you know the decision you are trying to make
      but do not yet know which topic hub should own that journey.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      This page is the top routing layer for the site-level cluster structure and is kept in sync with the current trust pages.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/topics/debt-to-income">DTI topic</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">Rent vs buy topic</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="Site-level topic routing, overlap clarification, and the editorial logic used to send readers into the correct decision workflow."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Choose the finance decision before you choose the topic</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Topic hubs work best when each one owns a distinct decision job. Start by naming the real finance question, then open the topic
      page built for that specific comparison path.
    </p>
    <div style="overflow:auto; margin-top:12px">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Your real decision</th>
            <th>Best topic hub</th>
            <th>Best starting tool</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>compare loan offers with fees or credits</td>
            <td><a href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a></td>
            <td><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>credit card payoff speed, minimum-payment drag, or payoff strategy</td>
            <td><a href="/topics/credit-cards">Credit cards topic</a></td>
            <td><a href="/calculators/credit-card-payoff-calculator">Credit card payoff calculator</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>housing affordability, DTI, or payment-fit questions</td>
            <td><a href="/topics/debt-to-income">Debt-to-income topic</a></td>
            <td><a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>renting versus buying over a planned hold period</td>
            <td><a href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">Rent vs buy topic</a></td>
            <td><a href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>mortgage payoff acceleration with extra principal</td>
            <td><a href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a></td>
            <td><a href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>refinance break-even, closing costs, or rate-reset decisions</td>
            <td><a href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic</a></td>
            <td><a href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Refinance break-even</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When topics overlap</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Choose <a href="/topics/debt-to-income">DTI</a> when the question is qualification or payment fit. Choose <a href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">rent vs buy</a> when the real job is comparing two housing paths over time.</li>
      <li>Choose <a href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">mortgage payoff</a> when you are adding principal to the current loan. Choose <a href="/topics/refinance">refinance</a> when you may replace the loan itself.</li>
      <li>Choose <a href="/topics/apr">APR</a> when you are comparing borrowing cost. Choose <a href="/topics/refinance">refinance</a> when timing, closing costs, and hold period are part of the full decision.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <a class="card section prose col-6" href="/topics/apr">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">APR and borrowing costs</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use this topic when the real question is whether fees, points, credits, or term differences change which loan is cheaper.
      </p>
    </a>
    <a class="card section prose col-6" href="/topics/credit-cards">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Credit cards and payoff strategy</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use this topic when the real question is payoff speed, minimum-payment drag, interest cost, or debt-order strategy.
      </p>
    </a>
    <a class="card section prose col-6" href="/topics/debt-to-income">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Debt-to-income and affordability</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use this topic when the real question is how lenders count debts and income, how much payment fits, or how to improve DTI before applying.
      </p>
    </a>
    <a class="card section prose col-6" href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Rent vs buy decisions</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use this topic when the real question is break-even timing, upfront cash, ownership costs, or assumption sensitivity across two housing paths.
      </p>
    </a>
    <a class="card section prose col-6" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Mortgage payoff and extra principal</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use this topic when the real question is whether extra monthly, lump-sum, or biweekly principal changes payoff speed enough to matter.
      </p>
    </a>
    <a class="card section prose col-6" href="/topics/refinance">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Refinance decisions</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Use this topic when the real question is break-even timing, term reset, cash-to-close, or whether a refinance beats staying put.
      </p>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to get better answers from any topic</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Start with one clean baseline using current statement or disclosure numbers.</li>
      <li>Change one assumption at a time so the comparison stays interpretable.</li>
      <li>Use the topic hub first when multiple calculators or guides could plausibly fit the same question.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How this routing layer is maintained</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      We maintain this page as the primary topic-entry layer for the active finance clusters so stronger starting points, overlap rules,
      and next-step boundaries stay aligned with the live calculators and support guides.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Request a topic</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If a finance question keeps falling between clusters, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> so we can decide
      whether it needs a stronger topic hub or a better support page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Updates</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      This routing page is updated when topic ownership changes, stronger entry paths are added, or overlap between clusters needs to be clarified.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-06-24</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
